  "query_preview": "..\nThe surface trough extending from Tropical Storm Saudel is slowly \nmoving out of the Marianas with some scattered locally heavy showers \nand isolated thunderstorms remaining. Showers and isolated \nthunderstorms are expected to become isolated tomorrow for Guam with \ncoverage remaining low-end scattered for Tinian and Saipan. A col \nlooks to develop over the region Friday ahead of current Tropical \nStorm Saudel, which will likely allow for potential island-effect \nshowers and isolated thunderstorms, particularly over Guam. By \nFriday night or Saturday, winds will begin picking back up as Saudel \napproaches. Current model guidance continues to indicate a passage \nthrough the far northern Marianas, placing Guam and the CNMI within \nits monsoonal tail. Thus, elevated winds, increasing showers, and \nthunderstorms are a possibility from the weekend through midweek. \nResidents of the Marianas should continue to monitor the forecast.",
